1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:07,714
In the green hills of West Java, there is a mountain that some say hides the oldest pyramid on Earth.

2
00:00:07,714 --> 00:00:08,957
Older than Egypt.

3
00:00:08,957 --> 00:00:10,711
Older than Göbekli Tepe.

4
00:00:10,711 --> 00:00:13,049
Twenty-seven thousand years old.

5
00:00:13,049 --> 00:00:15,900
Then the paper that said so was pulled.

6
00:00:16,366 --> 00:00:18,059
Today we do not argue.

7
00:00:18,059 --> 00:00:18,598
We dig.

8
00:00:18,598 --> 00:00:22,907
One layer at a time, we ask the stone what it can prove.

9
00:00:22,907 --> 00:00:24,600
This is Gunung Padang.

10
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:26,025
Gunung Padang.

11
00:00:26,025 --> 00:00:27,670
Evidence against theory.

12
00:00:27,670 --> 00:00:28,766
Start the drill.

13
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:32,273
Karyamukti village, near Cianjur, West Java.

14
00:00:32,273 --> 00:00:42,566
A hill about eight hundred and eighty-five meters high, with five terraces climbing its summit, and a stair of three hundred and seventy stone steps.

15
00:00:47,033 --> 00:00:52,673
The stair is steep, around forty-five degrees, about a hundred meters long.

16
00:00:52,673 --> 00:00:59,666
At the top, rows of dark stone columns line the terraces, laid flat, like a giant's woodpile.

17
00:01:00,133 --> 00:01:05,715
The columns are andesite, one to three meters long, many with five or six sides.

18
00:01:05,715 --> 00:01:09,134
Whoever arranged them did not have to carve them.

19
00:01:09,134 --> 00:01:10,599
They came ready-made.

20
00:01:11,066 --> 00:01:19,039
Local legend says King Siliwangi tried to build a palace here in a single night, and the sunrise caught him unfinished.

21
00:01:19,039 --> 00:01:20,714
A folktale, not evidence.

22
00:01:20,714 --> 00:01:24,400
But it shows people have known this hill for centuries.

23
00:01:24,866 --> 00:01:29,057
In eighteen ninety, a Dutch official named De Corte visited.

24
00:01:29,057 --> 00:01:35,342
A year later, the scholar Verbeek wrote it up: four terraces, with mounds probably graves.

25
00:01:35,342 --> 00:01:38,066
A site for the ancestors, nothing more.

26
00:01:38,533 --> 00:01:40,524
Then the jungle took it back.

27
00:01:40,524 --> 00:01:43,477
A report in nineteen fourteen, and silence.

28
00:01:43,477 --> 00:01:52,266
Local farmers rediscovered the stones in nineteen seventy-nine, and by nineteen ninety-eight it was protected as local heritage.

29
00:01:52,733 --> 00:01:57,691
So far, a megalithic temple, probably a few hundred years old or more.

30
00:01:57,691 --> 00:02:00,099
Nobody was talking about pyramids.

31
00:02:00,099 --> 00:02:02,366
That changed in the twenty-tens.

32
00:02:02,833 --> 00:02:05,852
Enter geologist Danny Hilman Natawidjaja.

33
00:02:05,852 --> 00:02:09,975
He saw something under the terraces: a buried structure.

34
00:02:09,975 --> 00:02:16,233
Not a hill with a temple on it, he argued, but a pyramid with the hill built into it.

35
00:02:16,699 --> 00:02:23,298
His team used ground-penetrating radar, electrical resistivity and seismic tomography.

36
00:02:23,298 --> 00:02:27,134
The scans showed layers, chambers, maybe a hollow.

37
00:02:27,134 --> 00:02:29,666
A pyramid buried inside the hill.

38
00:02:30,133 --> 00:02:36,682
Pyramid claim number one: an interior with man-made layers, descending for dozens of meters.

39
00:02:36,682 --> 00:02:38,533
A giant, hidden structure.

40
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,063
The idea grew.

41
00:02:40,063 --> 00:02:43,404
A presidential task force backed excavation.

42
00:02:43,404 --> 00:02:46,366
Thirty-four scholars signed a petition.

43
00:02:46,366 --> 00:02:48,796
Volunteers streamed to the site.

44
00:02:48,796 --> 00:02:53,733
For a moment, it felt like Indonesia might rewrite world history.

45
00:02:54,199 --> 00:02:59,052
But archaeology moves by trenches and by dates, so we follow the dates.

46
00:02:59,052 --> 00:03:00,966
This is where it gets sharp.

47
00:03:01,433 --> 00:03:03,410
Layer one: the mainstream date.

48
00:03:03,410 --> 00:03:05,133
The stone that you can see.

49
00:03:05,599 --> 00:03:12,875
Archaeologist Lutfi Yondri dates the visible structure to the second to fifth century of our era.

50
00:03:12,875 --> 00:03:16,324
Harry Truman Simanjuntak says sixth to eighth.

51
00:03:16,324 --> 00:03:20,449
Pottery found there ranges from about forty-five B.C.E.

52
00:03:20,449 --> 00:03:21,800
to twenty-two C.E.

53
00:03:22,266 --> 00:03:32,349
So the visible temple belongs to a society that built stone terraces for ancestor worship, like other megalithic sites in Indonesia.

54
00:03:32,349 --> 00:03:33,572
Impressive, yes.

55
00:03:33,572 --> 00:03:35,099
Ancient pyramid, no.

56
00:03:35,566 --> 00:03:41,799
In two thousand fourteen, the site became a national heritage area of twenty-nine hectares.

57
00:03:41,799 --> 00:03:46,800
Excavation halted that October after critics called the digging improper.

58
00:03:47,266 --> 00:03:49,056
Layer two: the rock itself.

59
00:03:49,056 --> 00:03:53,033
And here the pyramid story meets a different kind of expert.

60
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:59,725
Geologists Sutikno Bronto and Mohammad Langi studied the hill in twenty-seventeen.

61
00:03:59,725 --> 00:04:08,533
The top is an andesite porphyry intrusion, with natural columnar jointing, the way cooling lava cracks into columns.

62
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:12,568
You have seen this at Giant's Causeway in Ireland.

63
00:04:12,568 --> 00:04:13,996
Nobody builds those.

64
00:04:13,996 --> 00:04:19,064
Cooling rock does, and it splits into pillars one to three meters long.

65
00:04:19,064 --> 00:04:22,133
Which is exactly what lies on the terraces.

66
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:28,736
The intrusion itself was dated by potassium-argon: about thirty-two million years old.

67
00:04:28,736 --> 00:04:32,233
That is the age of the rock, not of any building.

68
00:04:32,699 --> 00:04:36,858
What about the glue between the stones, the so-called mortar?

69
00:04:36,858 --> 00:04:39,244
Bronto and Langi found clay crusts.

70
00:04:39,244 --> 00:04:41,766
Natural weathering rinds, not cement.

71
00:04:42,233 --> 00:04:52,641
Their picture: the neck of an ancient volcano, hydrothermally altered at the base, with a summit that collapsed in landslides in the late Pleistocene.

72
00:04:52,641 --> 00:04:56,666
A broken volcano with a temple placed on its best columns.

73
00:04:57,133 --> 00:05:02,507
So the rock explains the columns, the terraces' shape and the weak interior.

74
00:05:02,507 --> 00:05:04,628
It does not explain a pyramid.

75
00:05:04,628 --> 00:05:05,193
Not yet.

76
00:05:05,193 --> 00:05:06,466
Time for the core.

77
00:05:06,933 --> 00:05:09,833
Layer three: the cores that changed the headlines.

78
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:16,840
The Hilman team drilled into the hill and sent organic samples to be dated by radiocarbon.

79
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:22,800
The results were dramatic: soil from deep layers dating to thousands of years old.

80
00:05:23,266 --> 00:05:35,271
They said the layers were laid by humans: a first stage nine thousand years ago, a layer at sixteen thousand, and the deepest stage up to twenty-seven thousand years ago.

81
00:05:35,271 --> 00:05:36,966
During the last ice age.

82
00:05:37,433 --> 00:05:44,320
In October twenty-twenty-three, the claim appeared in the journal Archaeological Prospection.

83
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:48,985
Headlines went global: Indonesia's pyramid, the world's oldest.

84
00:05:48,985 --> 00:05:50,466
Social media agreed.

85
00:05:50,933 --> 00:05:53,393
Then the specialists read the methods.

86
00:05:53,393 --> 00:05:59,866
Critics asked: were the dated samples from the pyramid, or just from soil that happened to be there?

87
00:06:00,333 --> 00:06:01,567
Here is the key.

88
00:06:01,567 --> 00:06:06,195
Radiocarbon dates a piece of carbon, not an act of building.

89
00:06:06,195 --> 00:06:11,749
Soil on a volcano gets burned by fires, mixed by roots, moved by slides.

90
00:06:11,749 --> 00:06:15,066
Old carbon does not prove old construction.

91
00:06:15,533 --> 00:06:21,535
On the eighteenth of March, twenty-twenty-four, publisher Wiley retracted the paper.

92
00:06:21,535 --> 00:06:30,966
Reason: the radiocarbon samples were from soil not reliably linked to artifacts or features, so a human origin could not be assumed.

93
00:06:31,433 --> 00:06:38,617
The retraction notice said the interpretation of the data, that these were man-made layers, was incorrect.

94
00:06:38,617 --> 00:06:43,633
The twenty-seven-thousand-year headline lost its footing in one paragraph.

95
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:45,701
Hilman did not back down.

96
00:06:45,701 --> 00:06:56,399
He argued that the layers were still structured, that the cores sat inside the buried body, and that the retraction was about method, not the existence of a structure.

97
00:06:56,866 --> 00:06:58,563
Radar does show layers.

98
00:06:58,563 --> 00:07:00,113
Nobody disputes that.

99
00:07:00,113 --> 00:07:10,000
The dispute is what the layers are: stacked human work, or natural bands of lava, ash and weathered rock that volcanoes make for free.

100
00:07:10,466 --> 00:07:13,188
Volcanic hills are layered by nature.

101
00:07:13,188 --> 00:07:15,469
Every eruption leaves a stripe.

102
00:07:15,469 --> 00:07:20,766
A radar picture of stripes cannot, alone, tell a pyramid from a volcano.

103
00:07:21,233 --> 00:07:24,403
And here is the awkward part for the pyramid.

104
00:07:24,403 --> 00:07:26,728
The ancient dates came from soil.

105
00:07:26,728 --> 00:07:31,800
No tool, no pottery, no worked stone has been tied to those deep layers.

106
00:07:32,266 --> 00:07:38,738
People compare it with Göbekli Tepe, the real twelve-thousand-year-old temple in Turkey.

107
00:07:38,738 --> 00:07:46,533
But that site has carved pillars, animal reliefs and tools, all excavated and dated from the stone itself.

108
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:56,093
Indonesia does have real megalithic terraces: Pugung Raharja in Sumatra, Leuwiliang and Cibedug in West Java.

109
00:07:56,093 --> 00:08:02,100
Built by Austronesian-era communities, a few thousand years old at most.

110
00:08:02,566 --> 00:08:10,661
That fits Gunung Padang better: builders picked ready-made columns off the hill and stacked them into walls.

111
00:08:10,661 --> 00:08:12,535
Smart, effective, sacred.

112
00:08:12,535 --> 00:08:15,233
But not a lost ice-age civilization.

113
00:08:15,699 --> 00:08:20,360
Twenty-seven thousand years ago was the peak of the last ice age.

114
00:08:20,360 --> 00:08:22,869
Humans were hunting in small bands.

115
00:08:22,869 --> 00:08:27,100
No farms, no cities, no known way to stack a hill of stone.

116
00:08:27,566 --> 00:08:39,533
Which is why most archaeologists say the same thing: a real, remarkable temple, built over centuries, with sacred meaning, on top of a volcano that made its own stone.

117
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,019
What about the alien version?

118
00:08:42,019 --> 00:08:47,590
Some online claims say a lost advanced race, even visitors from space, built it.

119
00:08:47,590 --> 00:08:54,066
There is nothing at the site to support that: no machinery, no unknown metal, no inscription.

120
00:08:54,533 --> 00:08:56,582
The truth is more interesting.

121
00:08:56,582 --> 00:09:01,021
A natural wonder was shaped by people who understood its columns.

122
00:09:01,021 --> 00:09:07,100
We do not need aliens to explain it, and we do not need a lie about its age to admire it.

123
00:09:07,566 --> 00:09:09,923
Could something be buried deeper?

124
00:09:09,923 --> 00:09:10,566
Possibly.

125
00:09:10,566 --> 00:09:13,780
A new, properly documented dig could test it.

126
00:09:13,780 --> 00:09:17,066
Until that happens, deep claims stay unproven.

127
00:09:17,533 --> 00:09:18,984
Time to score the core.

128
00:09:18,984 --> 00:09:21,633
Evidence on one side, theory on the other.

129
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:27,773
A real terraced temple, five levels, three hundred and seventy steps: evidence.

130
00:09:27,773 --> 00:09:33,447
Natural columnar jointing of a thirty-two-million-year-old intrusion: evidence.

131
00:09:33,447 --> 00:09:37,899
Pottery and mainstream dates in the early centuries: evidence.

132
00:09:38,366 --> 00:09:42,118
A buried pyramid with chambers: not demonstrated.

133
00:09:42,118 --> 00:09:47,707
Man-made layers twenty-seven thousand years old: the paper was retracted.

134
00:09:47,707 --> 00:09:50,999
Aliens or a lost civilization: no evidence.

135
00:09:51,466 --> 00:09:52,371
The verdict.

136
00:09:52,371 --> 00:09:57,800
Gunung Padang is a genuine megalithic temple on a natural volcanic hill.

137
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,836
The world's oldest pyramid?

138
00:09:59,836 --> 00:10:02,399
Not on the evidence we have today.

139
00:10:02,866 --> 00:10:08,366
But one thing stays true: a retraction is not a final answer, it is a challenge.

140
00:10:08,366 --> 00:10:10,566
Better evidence could change it.

141
00:10:10,566 --> 00:10:13,866
Good detectives stay open, and follow the proof.

142
00:10:14,333 --> 00:10:20,299
Next time, we cross the ocean to another stone mystery that seems too old to be true.

143
00:10:20,299 --> 00:10:22,966
Subscribe so you do not miss the case.

144
00:10:23,433 --> 00:10:25,725
So, what do you think the hill is hiding?

145
00:10:25,725 --> 00:10:27,066
Tell us in the comments.
